	<td width="14" style="background-image:url(/skins/north_qeynos2_1/images/box/left.gif); background-repeat:repeat-y;"><img src="/skins/north_qeynos2_1/images/box/left.gif" width="14" height="100%"></td>
	<td width="100%" align="left" valign="top">
		This is the quest that you must complete to gain access to the Feerrott before attaining level 42. It is given at level 37. Qeynos players will receive this quest from Boulden Smitestone in the Qeynos Harbor, where Freeport players receive it from Slaughtergrott the Vigilant at the docks in East Freeport. The quest journal gives very vague information throughout this quest, but we&#39;ll guide you through it. <br /><br />The first order of business is to search Zek, the Orcish Wastes for someone who might know something. Near the Vallon Foundry (mines, sort of in middle of the map) you will find an Orc Cartographer and his bodyguards pathing around outside. Kill them. <br /><br />You will notice after the others fall that the Orc Cartographer is now a hailable NPC. Speak to him and he will fess up some information. <br /><br />You must now elminiate the Catapult threat. You do this by killing three groups of Tallon Catapult Operators near the docks. You must clear three different groups of them. <br /><br />After this has been done you must find and kill General Lutzgorg in Zek. General Lutzgorg is a triggered spawn when you go near the building at -470, -298, -290. He is level 40 with some berserker guards. <br /><br />After killing him it&#39;s time to head to the docks in Thundering Steppes. This is where things get separate a little. If you are a mixed good and evil group things get bugged here but there is a workaround for this that we&#39;ll discuss below. <br /><br />Good players are supposed to speak to Boulden Smitestone at the docks, where evils speak to Slaughtergrott the Vigilant. After doing this you are supposed to click the bell to Feerrott at the docks to be teleported to a special instanced zone which is similar to the other boat ride access quests in the game. Both are the same zone basically, with the only exception being that Slaughtergrott is on the evil boat and Boulden is on the good boat. In a all good or all evil expedition you can just hail them on the boat then complete the boat trial and speak to them to exit and get teleported to the Feerrott with access. <br /><br />The boat trial is pretty easy. Boulden or Slaughtergrott willl begin casting a spell, which takes about 10 minutes to cast. You simply keep the monsters from killing them during that time (which is pretty easy). Eventually they will cast the spell and the monsters will despawn. You then hail them to teleport to the Feerrott. <br /><br />If you are in a mixed group though you will have to use the following workaround... First everyone will have to disband and click the bell solo. Once inside they talk to Boulden or Slaughtergrott to advance their quest. They then kill them to be teleported out (any time they die the trial ends). You then regroup at the docks and you do one boat at a time. You will have to do both the good and evil this way. After the good boat is finished good players can hail Boulden to gain access, after the evil boat is finished evil players can hail Slaughtergrott to finish.
