	<td width="14" style="background-image:url(/skins/north_qeynos2_1/images/box/left.gif); background-repeat:repeat-y;"><img src="/skins/north_qeynos2_1/images/box/left.gif" width="14" height="100%"></td>
	<td width="100%" align="left" valign="top">
		<p>This quest is given by Arqis in Nektulos. He is located near the bridge to Commonlands. Completing it gives you access to the raid zone: Cauldron Hollow. <br /><br />The first order of duty is to find a book about Cauldron Hollow. This book can be found in a stack of books that is resting on a table at the Academy in North Freeport (+10.92, -7, -128.22), or in the Three Towers in South Qeynos, opposite from Sage Indis Surion (need loc). Right click it and inspect it to get a list of books in this stack. Read the Vanishing of Cauldron Hollow book. You can also read the other book to open up another quest. <br /><br />After reading the book you should return to Arqis in Nektulos Forest. <br /><br />Arqis will refer you to Dalninia, the Fairy in Nektulos Forest. Dalninia can be found at -196, 0, -342. <br /><br />Dalninia will ask you to visit Queen Thayilia. Queen Thayilia is another fairy in the Nektulos Forest. She can be found at -499, +2, -292. She will ask you to slay Queen Dyleena. <br /><br />Queen Dyleena can be foud near the bone lake, way up past the top of N&#39;Marr&#39;s Ascent. To easily get Queen Dyleena solo, just pull her to the edge of the lake with non damage. For example, just pull with taunt, and run to the lake. Her protectors wont follow if she isn&#39;t damaged, and if you get to the edge of the lake, she is out of range of her helpers. <br /><br />After killing Queen Dyleena, go back and talk to Queen Thayilia, then Dalninia. Dalninia tells you you have to go and enter the Funeral Pyre (-960, +12, -715) and kill its 3 guardians. The 3 guardians will spawn if you walk near the Pyre. Kill them, walk into the Pyre, and you&#39;ll be sent to go back and talk to Arqis. <br /><br />Arqis tells you you must now light the Torches of Forewarning. To do this, you must visit the named treant Rulinthus who is quite near the Fire Guard (the wall that blocks lavastorm off at -47, +92, -2028), right at the north end of Nektulos. If you go to the Fire Guard then go west a little, you&#39;ll find a druid ring with Rulinthus standing in the middle (and a lot of aggro bats). Talk to him, and he sends you to kill Tilberbous. <br /><br />Tillberbous is found in the East of Nektulos, fairly near the road. Follow the road through wisp territory, take the right fork, and you&#39;ll get to an area with a lot of skeletons. If you look South while heading along the road, you&#39;ll see him. After killing Tillerbous, you must go back to Rulinthus. <br /><br />Rulinthus gives you the twig which can be used to light the torches of forewarning, and the Gates of Cauldron Hollow quest finishes. Examining and snapping the twig that Rulinthus gave you will trigger another Access Quest &quot;Cauldron Hollow: Lighting the Torches of Forewarning&quot;.</p><p /><p><strong><u>PART 2</u></strong></p><p>This is the second part of hte Cauldron Hollow access quest. It is initiated by examining the Twig of Rulinthus. This is rewarded to you at the end of the Gates of Cauldron Hollow quest (see related quests). <br /><br />The new quest requires you to light the torches from the gates of neriak to end of the river. The first torch is at the Dragoon/Thexian camp in the NE of zone, where the Shiny Brass Halberd quest comes from. Follow the road through wisp land, turn left, and follow all the way to the end. The torch at the entrance of the camp there is the first torch. Now run all the way back down the road, touching each torch as you pass, and your quest will update to &quot;approach the 13th torch of forewarning&quot; etc. As you light the final torch, which is near the bridge to Commonlands, the quest will change to tell you to slay the 3 Generals and take their keys to Cauldron Hollow. The first is found on the broken bridge, the second is at the top of N&#39;Mars ascent, and the third is in the canyon leading to the beach. <br /><br />Once you kill the third general, the quest is done and you finally have access to Cauldron Hollows, which is a 2-3 group raid zone accessible from the door at the North end of the beach.</p>
